-From 3ed82f01aeda94d079810d0baba70a54b5cd8392 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
-From: Ai-Semo0o DevOps <devops@ai-semo0o.local>
-Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 05:37:43 +0000
-Subject: [PATCH] fix(db): make SQLite path resilient to unwritable /var/data
- (Render Free EACCES)
-
-Root cause
-- backend/db/client.mjs blindly ran mkdirSync(path.dirname(DATABASE_FILE))
-  at construction time. On Render's Free plan there is no persistent disk,
-  so /var/data is never mounted and is not writable, which aborted boot with
-  'EACCES: permission denied, mkdir /var/data/db'.
-
-Fix
-- Resolve the SQLite path defensively (resolveDatabaseFile): probe the nearest
-  existing ancestor for writability BEFORE creating anything, then walk an
-  ordered fallback chain: DATABASE_FILE -> DATABASE_DIR -> ./backend/data ->
-  os.tmpdir(). Never mkdir a non-writable fixed path; log a warning on fallback.
-- New optional DATABASE_DIR env var (directory instead of full file path).
-- Preserve the 0700 directory / 0600 file privacy guarantees and every schema,
-  migration and tenant/project isolation rule (migrate() unchanged).
-- server.mjs: bind 0.0.0.0 whenever PORT is set (Render/Railway/Fly/Cloud Run),
-  keep loopback for local dev, allow BIND_HOST override; clearer startup log.
-- render.yaml: default to the Free plan with the persistent disk commented out;
-  document how to re-enable persistence on a paid plan.
-- backend/.env.example + DEPLOY_AR.md: document the fallback behaviour.
-- backend/test/db-path.test.mjs: 4 regression tests for the fallback logic.
-
-Tests
-- node --experimental-sqlite --test backend/test/*.mjs -> 49/49 pass.
-- Live boot with read-only /var/data + DATABASE_FILE=/var/data/db/agent.sqlite
-  -> logs fallback, listens on 0.0.0.0, GET /health -> 200 (no EACCES).
