-+# HOW TO USE
-+#   1. Push this repository to GitHub.
-+#   2. Render Dashboard -> New -> Blueprint -> pick this repo.
-+#   3. Render reads this file and creates the service.
-+#   4. Fill the secret env vars in the dashboard (SECRETS_MASTER_KEY, ...).
-+#
-+# FREE vs PAID (read this — it is why the app used to crash on Free)
-+# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-+# The Free plan has NO persistent disk, so `/var/data` is never mounted and is
-+# NOT writable. The old configuration pointed DATABASE_FILE at
-+# `/var/data/db/agent.sqlite`, and the database client blindly tried to
-+# `mkdir /var/data/db`, which aborted the process at boot with:
-+#     EACCES: permission denied, mkdir '/var/data/db'
-+# The database client is now defensive: it verifies that the target directory is
-+# writable and, if not, automatically falls back to a writable location
-+# (./backend/data/agent.sqlite, then the OS temp dir). So this blueprint boots on
-+# the Free plan out of the box — the SQLite file just lives on the ephemeral
-+# filesystem (data is reset on every deploy).
-+#
-+# To KEEP the database across deploys, use a paid plan and re-enable the
-+# persistent disk: set `plan:` to `starter` (or higher) and uncomment the `disk:`
-+# block at the bottom of this file.
-+# =============================================================================
